    <worksheet name='Deaths Per 100,000 by State'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>U.S. Drug-Induced Overdose Deaths Involving Any Opioid, Per 100,000 By State, 1999-2020</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Includes opioid-related overdose deaths with underlying cause of </run>
            <run italic='true'>drug-induced causes</run>
            <run>Æ </run>
            <run italic='true'>(unintentional, suicide, homicide, undetermined, etc)</run>
            <run> as categorized in the International Classification of Diseases (ICD-10). 

</run>
            <run italic='true'>Any opioid</run>
            <run>, as identified by the ICD-10 multiple cause of death includes the following: Heroin (T40.1), Other opioids (T40.2), Methadone (T40.3), Other synthetic opioids other than methadone (T40.4 - fentanyl, tramadol, etc), Other unspecified opioids (T40.6)

Source: </run>
            <run auto-url='true' hyperlink='tabdoc:load-url url=&amp;quot;https://wonder.cdc.gov/&amp;quot;'>https://wonder.cdc.gov/</run>
            <run>Æ </run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
